<Layout title="Terms · Dipity" description="The terms for using Dipity.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto px-5 pt-10 sm:px-8">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These terms cover your use of the Dipity app, made by Coracle Social LLC ("Coracle", "we"). By using Dipity you agree to
      them. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Effective October 7, 2026.</strong></p>

    <h2>What Dipity is</h2>
    <p>
      Dipity is software that runs on your phone and exchanges posts directly with other phones
      nearby. There is no Dipity service in the middle. We don't host, receive, review or store
      anything you or anyone else posts. Each person's phone holds and shares content on its own.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      What you post is yours, and you are responsible for it. By posting, you understand that your
      post is handed to the phones your settings allow, that those people can keep and copy it, and
      that it can't be fully withdrawn once shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Please don't use Dipity to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break the law, or encourage anyone else to;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten, impersonate or stalk anyone;</li>
      <li>share content that exploits or endangers children;</li>
      <li>share nudity, sexual content or graphic violence;</li>
      <li>share other people's private information without their permission;</li>
      <li>flood your neighbours with spam, or interfere with other people's phones.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because there's no central service, we can't remove content from other people's phones or
      suspend anyone's account. The tools for keeping your board pleasant are in your hands: you can
      mute, block or forget anyone, and choose whose posts your phone accepts.
    </p>

    <h2>Your key</h2>
    <p>
      Your identity is a key stored on your phone. Nobody, including us, can recover it for you if
      it's lost, or revoke it if it's stolen. Keeping it safe, and backed up if you want to, is up to
      you.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Dipity is provided as it is, without warranties of any kind. We don't promise that it will
      always work, that posts will reach anyone in particular, or that it will be free of errors.
      Delivery depends on Bluetooth, on phones being near each other, and on the people who carry
